changes:
  - path: docs/use-cases/web-ui.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "Both native contracts this epic touched, as they now stand. UC-4 gains three observable capabilities: the list states a core that is not answering - above rows it does not discard, naming the address, offering a retry, and appearing with the user doing nothing because the dropped SSE stream is the signal; a refused query quotes the value it refused, in the row region, with no retry, and never beside the connection statement, since an API that answers and says no is a different fact from one that does not answer; and a long value is readable further because the pane is a chosen width. Its filter sentence now reads the status parameter at either resolution - 404 the exact code, 4xx the class, anything naming neither refused as a stated 400 - and the stale clause promising the control would catch up with the core is gone, because it did. UC-5 gains raw | pretty as the terms its switch settles on and the observable half of the width. UC-ONBOARD is deliberately untouched: E-ONBOARD restates the contract it changes. v5 -> v7."
  - path: docs/decisions/dec-35-citations-resolve-or-fail.html
    tier: T2
    action: added
    distills: "A docstring citation resolves against the tree or it fails a test (W2). DEC-16 makes a built component's TSDoc its retired design file, so an entry naming deleted code is the contract lying - and seven such claims across five of the 28 entries had survived a design run, a Tier-3 review and a merge gate. What may resolve is derived from the tree, never transcribed: there is no allowlist, which is the rejected option and the one the next annoyed reader will reach for."
  - path: docs/decisions/dec-36-the-pane-and-the-window.html
    tier: T2
    action: added
    distills: "The pane width and the window are one decision (W4 designed, W6 built): 520px in a window that opens at 1440, on the identity path = window - pane - 612, because every pixel the pane takes comes out of the list's one unbounded column. Six rejected alternatives, each with the number that killed it, including the bounded share min(40%, 520px) that was measured rather than argued. Carries the consequence the run refused to hide: no valid arrangement below 1132px with the pane open, up from 992, against a declared minimum window of 800 - a known defect this epic made wider, deliberately, with the arithmetic published."
  - path: docs/decisions/dec-34-fixed-height-rows-truncate.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "The criterion for the second sighting its own consequences had asked for and never defined: mono, inert, unbounded, visibly cut - all four - plus the candidate W4 tested and refused, since the identity bar wanted CopyText because a pane has height to spend. The three conditions and the escape are untouched."
  - path: docs/decisions/dec-31-leg-is-panel-scoped.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "The cell describing what the body pane owns names the shipped positions, raw | pretty. An incidental description of the pane's copy; the leg-scoping ruling stands."
  - path: docs/decisions/dec-32-body-is-the-main-zone.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "The panel sketch's control row re-aligned to the shipped labels, and one line naming which pane the record's numbers were written against now that DEC-36 has moved it. The zoning ruling is untouched - a wider pane moves the clamp's cost, it does not remove it."
  - path: docs/decisions/decisions-index.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "Rows for DEC-35 and DEC-36, because T2 is read index-first and an unindexed record does not exist; DEC-32's summary gains the same 'pane of the time' qualifier as the record. v15 -> v17."
